  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">In ball culture, ballroom families (or houses) are chosen families headed by and named after established community members (e.g., the House of Xtravaganza); heads of ballroom families are typically called "mothers" or "fathers," while members are termed "children" and "siblings."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="680" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
